      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Adding onto this: Maybe voice priority can override the radius of earmuff mode. So even if my friend is outside the boundary of earmuff mode, i can still hear them. It would even solve my prior issue of earmuff modes radius \"not quite cutting it\".",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-11-14T20:03:08.396Z",
  "deleteID": null,
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "In crowded instances, I often am drowned out by the noise, voices, and music playing. I spend more time adjusting the volume sliders for each individual person, and the world, and the overall master volume, more than I am actually paying attention to my friends or my environment. It can be quite overstimulating. While Earmuff mode is helpful, it's in a radius and sometimes a radius doesn't quite cut it. I would like a feature that allows \"Voice priority\" over some others. Say for example, I want to make sure I hear my friend incase they say something. I can turn on voice priority for them, and they will be louder than other sound sources. In a crowded room full of talking individuals, I can always hear my friend incase they are saying something to me. How to toggle this on/off and where it will be placed is up to the developers. But I think it will help especially for those with poor hearing, or akin to Auditory Processing Disorder.",
